WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.923
Got a Godot game? Ship it to WeChat, Douyin, and TikTok mini games, in one click.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:11.214
Until now, that meant custom engine builds, broken templates, and glue code.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.239
Now, it's just one panel.

4
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.468
Pick a platform, enter your App ID, and hit Export.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:25.586
You get the game pack, a mini-game engine, the adapters, and the platform config. No Node.js. No Emscripten.

6
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:35.031
Open the folder in the platform's DevTools, and it just runs. The engine is built for mini games, so it holds up on real phones, too.

7
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:44.225
Then call mini-game features right from GDScript: two hundred and twenty-five methods, and eighty-four signals, across all three platforms.

8
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:53.615
Every engine template matches your exact Godot version. Certified ones download, verify, and install in a single click.

9
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.893
Zero extra tools. Three platforms. One Godot project.

10
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:08.844
Godot Mini Game is free and open source. Check it out on GitHub, and if it helps you, give it a star.
